We can efficiently implement the feedforward (FF) and feedback (FB) form of inhibition without actually requiring the inhibitory interneurons, by using the average excitatory input ge and activity levels in a given layer, in a simple equation shown below. This works surprisingly well, without requiring subsequent parameter adaptation during learning, and this FFFB form of inhibition has now replaced the k-Winners-Take-All (kWTA) form of inhibition used in the 1st Edition of the textbook (O’Reilly and Munakata 2000).
